@Kelli

If your argument is that Hanukkah is a Hebrew festival because it’s a Hebrew word, then Hol is a Sanskrit festival. Actually, חנוכה is the Hebrew festival, so Hanukkah, as it is spelled in English, must be an English festival. And Janucá must be a Spanish festival. Also, Christmas must be an English festival, and Noël a French festival. 

The reality is that religious festivals are denoted by the religion, not a language. The fact that some Holi celebrants speak Hindi doesn’t make it a Hindi festival. If we go by etymology, it’s a Sanskrit festival, but really, it’s a Hindu festival.

